<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 89 0 R
/T (A. Understanding the Issue)
/E (A. Understanding the Issue)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
172 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
/E (The world faces a major energy and environmental challenge. Countries across Africa, Asia, Latin America, and parts of Europe continue to rely heavily on fossil fuels like coal, diesel, and biomass for electricity generation and household energy needs. This dependence has contributed to severe air pollution, greenhouse gas emissions, and major public health concerns.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
173 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
/E (At the same time, millions of people in rural and low-income communities still lack reliable access to electricity. Solar energy has emerged as a promising solution because large parts of the world receive abundant sunlight year-round. Solar power can reduce dependence on fossil fuels, improve air quality, and increase access to clean and affordable electricity.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
174 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
/E (However, equitable access remains a challenge. Wealthier urban populations and businesses are increasingly adopting solar technology, while poorer communities often struggle due to high installation costs, weak infrastructure, lack of financing, and limited awareness.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
175 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
/E (Clean energy is directly connected to climate change, economic development, public health, and global sustainability. Many regions of the world suffer from dangerous levels of air pollution, and improving access to renewable energy is essential to reducing pollution and achieving international climate goals.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
176 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
/E (Public Health: Air pollution causes millions of premature deaths annually.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
177 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
/E (Climate Change: Fossil fuels are a major source of greenhouse gas emissions.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
178 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
/E (Economic Development: Renewable energy can create green jobs and improve energy security.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
179 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
/E (Energy Equality: Solar energy can bring electricity to remote and underserved communities.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
180 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
/E (SDG 7: The UN aims to ensure affordable and clean energy for all by 2030.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
181 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
/E (These statistics highlight the strong connection between energy choices, economic growth, public health, and environmental sustainability.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
182 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 830 0 R
/E (Over 700 million people worldwide still lack access to electricity, mostly in Sub-Saharan Africa and parts of Asia.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
